{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "privacy.no_source_to_llm", "priority": 1000, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "PRIVACY BOUNDARY [R09]: Never send full source code to external LLM. Send only sanitized error messages, line numbers, RCA categories, and fix directives. Strip file paths, variable names, and business logic. The intelligence asset is the governed memory, not the vendor model.", "tags": ["privacy", "ownership", "llm-boundary", "R09"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "privacy.no_secrets_in_output", "priority": 1000, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "SECURITY [I6]: No secrets in repo. No API keys, passwords, tokens, IP addresses, or internal paths in generated code or logs. Use environment variables. No stack traces to external clients.", "tags": ["privacy", "security", "I6"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "privacy.sanitize_errors", "priority": 1000, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "repair", "content": "REPAIR PRIVACY [R06,R09]: Before sending errors to LLM, strip file paths, replace project-specific identifiers with generic placeholders, limit context to failing lines only. Every memory record must have provenance.", "tags": ["privacy", "repair", "provenance", "R06"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "memory.provenance_policy", "priority": 1000, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "learning", "content": "MEMORY GOVERNANCE [R06]: Demand provenance on every record. Expiry on aging facts. Correction workflow propagates. Conflict detection surfaced not averaged. Deletion actually deletes. Treat store like database with DBA.", "tags": ["memory", "governance", "R06"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.agent_ownership", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "OWNERSHIP [R02,I2]: One owner per unit of work. Language routing: Python=agents/intelligence, Go=transfer/network, Rust=compute/speed. If answer to who owns this is everyone you have an orphan.", "tags": ["ownership", "architecture", "R02", "I2"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.error_handling", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "ERROR CONTRACT [I3]: All cross-service failures MUST use ErrorEnvelope. Stable codes: VAL_, AUTH_, BIZ_, DEP_, RES_, NET_, INT_. Retry only when retryable=true. No panic/unwrap/expect/bare except/ignored err. Consumers key off code+retryable only.", "tags": ["errors", "contracts", "I3"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.contract_first", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "generation", "content": "CONTRACT FIRST [R04,I1]: Define API/message/error contracts before implementation. One tool layer called identically everywhere. Skills bolted onto unverified substrate industrialize errors.", "tags": ["architecture", "contracts", "R04", "I1"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.action_gate", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "ACTION GATE [R08]: Measure then Analyze then Act. Stage 1: every outward move behind a gate. Autonomy expanded per action type as auditable policy not a vibe. Irreversible actions are not callable tools.", "tags": ["governance", "safety", "R08"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.substrate_first", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "SUBSTRATE BEFORE SKILLS [R07]: Verify data layer before adding intelligence. If substrate lies every skill industrializes lying faster. Boring first then agents propose moves.", "tags": ["architecture", "R07"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.logging", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "OBSERVABILITY [I5]: Structured logs: service, trace_id, span_id, code, duration_ms. Context/deadline/cancellation propagates edge to leaf. Graceful shutdown. Health: liveness vs readiness separated.", "tags": ["logging", "observability", "I5"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "governance_rule", "key": "constitution.deterministic", "priority": 900, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "DETERMINISM: Same input equals same output. No random seeds without config. Idempotency required for writes. Deadlines propagate; remaining time honored [I5].", "tags": ["determinism", "testing", "I5"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "language_standard", "key": "rust.coding_standard", "priority": 800, "language": "rust", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "RUST STANDARDS [COMPUTE]: Result<T,E> on request path no unwrap/expect/panic. checked_add/checked_mul. thiserror for errors. Bounded channels. No hidden globals. Small functions under 50 lines. Clippy clean. Proper ownership/lifetime.", "tags": ["rust", "standards", "compute"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "language_standard", "key": "go.coding_standard", "priority": 800, "language": "go", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "GO STANDARDS [TRANSFER]: Percent-w wrapping on errors. context.Context on every RPC/IO. Client timeouts. No goroutine leaks. No ignored err. gofmt/go vet clean. Worker pools with backpressure. Graceful shutdown.", "tags": ["go", "standards", "transfer"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "language_standard", "key": "python.coding_standard", "priority": 800, "language": "python", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "PYTHON STANDARDS [INTELLIGENCE]: Type hints on all signatures. No bare except. No eval/exec. Explicit exception types. pathlib over os.path. dataclasses for structured data. logging not print. AppError domain exceptions. Deterministic tests.", "tags": ["python", "standards", "intelligence"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "language_standard", "key": "architecture.single_responsibility", "priority": 800, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "SINGLE RESPONSIBILITY [R05]: One bounded agent per credential set. Split only when tools permissions or evaluations diverge. Narrow agents have small blast radius. Fleet is destination not starting point.", "tags": ["architecture", "R05"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "language_standard", "key": "architecture.honest_failure", "priority": 800, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "*", "content": "HONEST FAILURE [R10]: Connectors self-test on load. Reports print caveats next to numbers. Failure states honest visible boring. Plan for connector failure enrichment mismatch agent reaching past brief.", "tags": ["architecture", "resilience", "R10"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "llm_interaction_rule", "key": "llm.generation_rules", "priority": 750, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "generation", "content": "GENERATION: Produce complete compilable code. All imports included. Follow language standards. Add structured logging. Handle all errors explicitly. No placeholder comments. No drive-by refactors. Match existing style.", "tags": ["llm", "generation"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "llm_interaction_rule", "key": "llm.repair_rules", "priority": 750, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "repair", "content": "REPAIR: Fix ONLY reported errors. Do not rewrite working code. Preserve style. Phase A compile errors first. Phase B after compile passes address warnings. Output complete file. Minimal diff. No unrelated cleanup.", "tags": ["llm", "repair"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "llm_interaction_rule", "key": "llm.delta_repair_rules", "priority": 750, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "delta_repair", "content": "DELTA REPAIR: You receive ONLY failing lines with plus-minus 3 context. Fix only those lines. Respond JSON with operations array and confidence float. Ops: replace_lines insert_after delete_lines append. Do NOT include code outside specified range. Preserve indentation.", "tags": ["llm", "delta_repair"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "llm_interaction_rule", "key": "llm.adversarial_rules", "priority": 750, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "adversarial", "content": "ADVERSARIAL REVIEW: You are a hostile reviewer. Find edge cases overflow risks security gaps missing error handling. Output JSON findings array. Each finding has severity description suggested_fix. Do NOT see source code only structural description and sanitized errors.", "tags": ["llm", "adversarial"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "learning_policy", "key": "learning.scorecard_policy", "priority": 650, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "learning", "content": "SCORECARD [R01]: Define metrics before building. Measure accuracy adoption hours-saved exception-rate. Agent saving 10 hours but shipping 1 wrong result is net negative. Scorecard must see both value and risk.", "tags": ["learning", "metrics", "R01"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "learning_policy", "key": "learning.anti_pattern_promotion", "priority": 650, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "learning", "content": "ANTI-PATTERN POLICY: When error repeats 2+ times with quality_delta=0 promote to anti-pattern. When strategy fails 3+ times switch strategy. Unknown category triggers RCA before storage. Never store source code.", "tags": ["learning", "anti-pattern"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
{"knowledge_type": "learning_policy", "key": "learning.strategy_switching", "priority": 650, "language": "*", "module_type": "*", "phase": "learning", "content": "STRATEGY SWITCHING: If same strategy produces quality_delta=0 for 2 consecutive attempts switch patch to rewrite or rewrite to patch. Delta repair attempted before full regeneration. Adversarial findings only after compile passes.", "tags": ["learning", "strategy"], "version": "1.0", "enabled": true, "_type": "knowledge"}
